::title::

# Finding the widest margin, step by step

::default::

<SvmSteps>

<template #step0="{ errors, nSV }">

A first guess: it points the right way, but it is rotated, off-centre, and its margin is narrow. **{{ errors }}** points sit on the wrong side.

Circled: the {{ nSV }} points that are misclassified or touch their margin line.

</template>

<template #default="{ step, steps, nSV, margin, final }">

<div v-if="!final">

Step {{ step }} of {{ steps }}: the line turns and the margin grows, moving points to the correct side.

Margin width: {{ margin }}. Still circled: {{ nSV }} points.

</div>

<div v-else>

**Done.** {{ margin }} is the widest margin that keeps every point out of the band.

The {{ nSV }} circled points sit exactly on its edges. These are the **support vectors**: they alone fix the line, and moving any other point changes nothing.

</div>

</template>

</SvmSteps>

